","type":"text"},{"code":"minimumSpanningTree(weight:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), a minimum-weight perfect matching on its odd-degree","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices (","type":"text"},{"code":"minimumWeightMatching","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), and an Eulerian circuit of their union by Hierholzer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from the first vertex, shortcut to the first visit of each vertex. The matching is on the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"complete graph of the odd vertices in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order (pairs i < j lexicographic), and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"circuit’s multigraph lists the tree edges by position, then the matched pairs in that order,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so the tour is determined. At most 3\/2 × the shortest tour when the weights satisfy the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"triangle inequality (not checked).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Tours read the simple graph, as ","type":"text"},{"code":"nearestNeighborTour(weight:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" documents; nil below three","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The graph is complete; the sum along a tour fits in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"W"},{"type":"text","text":". When "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"W"},{"type":"text","text":" is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FixedWidthInteger"},{"type":"text","text":", every non-loop edge’s weight satisfies n · (2 · |weight| + 1) ≤"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"W.max \/ 8"},{"type":"text","text":" (the matching’s bound), checked as each weight is read, so a weight beyond it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"traps even on an edge the matching never sees; so n ≤ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"W.max \/ 8"},{"type":"text","text":" (15 vertices for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int8"},{"type":"text","text":"), whatever the weights. An arbitrary-precision integer has no bound."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Precondition","style":"note"},{"type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(n³): the matching on up to n vertices; the tree O(n²)."}]}],"name":"Complexity","style":"note"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours","doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/tours\/graphprotocols\/graph\/christofidestour(weight:)-6qvc8"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Christofides’ tour (Christofides 1976; Serdyukov 1978)."}],"references":{"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph/Vertex":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"associatedtype","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph\/vertex","title":"Vertex","abstract":[]},"doc://Tours/documentation/Tours/GraphProtocols":{"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/tours\/graphprotocols","title":"GraphProtocols","abstract":[]},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph/Edges-swift.associatedtype":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges